# The patch files under patches/ are `git format-patch` output and are applied with
# `git apply`, which matches context lines byte for byte and verifies the blob index
# recorded in each header. A clone made with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite their
# line endings on checkout and every patch would then fail to apply, with an error
# ("patch does not apply") that points at the patch rather than at the clone. Mark
# them binary-ish so no EOL conversion is ever applied, on any platform.
patches/** -text

# Same reasoning for the signing keys and any PEM: byte-exact or useless.
*.pem -text
